#
# prefer_idle for the scheduler groups. The boost that belongs next to it is
# not here, and the reason is worth writing down.
#
# This kernel has SchedTune (CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE=y) and does not expose uclamp in
# the cgroups: /dev/cpuctl/*/cpu.uclamp.min does not exist. Up to Android 11
# AOSP set the /dev/stune boosts in init.rc; Android 12 dropped those lines
# because it moved to uclamp, so nobody raises the frequency for what the user
# is looking at. Apps do land in the right group -- task_profiles_29.json does
# that, and it is what the system loads since the vendor is API 29 -- but the
# group sits at boost=0.
#
# The obvious repair is to write schedtune.boost here. It does not work, and
# two attempts at making it work by retrying failed on 23.2: the value was
# always found back at zero on a booted phone. The reason is that the file is
# not a setting. On this SoC /dev/stune/<group>/schedtune.boost is the output
# of an arbitration inside the kernel, drivers/misc/mediatek/performance/
# boost_ctrl/eas_ctrl/, which recomputes it as the MAX over its kickers and
# writes the result. Every app launch triggers a recomputation, all kickers are
# zero, and zero is what lands in the file. Isolated by bisection: the value
# survives idling, a force-stop and any amount of scrolling, and dies exactly
# on am start.
#
# So the boost is set on the kernel side now, as a kicker, by the ta_boost_floor
# parameter of that driver. Being one term of a MAX it only raises the boost and
# never caps it, so the vendor perf service still wins when it asks for more.
#
# prefer_idle is a different matter: the arbitration does not touch it, it is
# measured to survive an app launch, and plain init writes make it stick -- that
# much was always true, and was the half of the old service that actually
# worked. Which is why there is no service here any more.

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    # What the user is looking at: idle cores, and the boost from the kernel.
    write /dev/stune/top-app/schedtune.prefer_idle 1

    # The rest of the foreground: no boost, but idle cores all the same.
    # Raising this one too is pointless, SystemUI is already in top-app.
    write /dev/stune/foreground/schedtune.prefer_idle 1

    write /dev/stune/rt/schedtune.prefer_idle 1
